        {
          "_key": "k000r9",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Meals all summer"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k000ra",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k000rb",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Summer days are long, so meals come at set times: breakfast from 7:30 to 9 am, lunch at 12 noon and a snack at 3 pm, plus dinner at 6 pm for kids who stay into the evening. Lunches are real meals, like arroz con pollo with brown rice or chicken fajitas with peppers, served through the USDA food program (CACFP)."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
